1
00:02:29,069 --> 00:02:29,963
<v MR THORNDYKE> Thorndyke’s

2
00:02:29,963 --> 00:02:33,082
<v EDITH> Good morning. Is that Mr Thorndyke?

3
00:02:33,082 --> 00:02:35,029
<v MR THORNDYKE> Speaking. How can I help?

4
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:42,382
<v EDITH> I’ve got quite a few things which need painting and fixing in the flat and I wonder whether you’d be able to do the work.

5
00:02:42,382 --> 00:02:46,113
<v MR THORNDYKE> I’m sure I’d be able to help but let me take down a few details.

6
00:02:46,113 --> 00:02:47,721
<v EDITH> Yes, of course.

7
00:02:47,721 --> 00:02:51,269
<v MR THORNDYKE> Well, firstly, how did you hear about us?

8
00:02:51,269 --> 00:02:58,206
<v EDITH> It was my friend May Hampton … you did some excellent work for her a couple of years ago. Do you remember?

9
00:02:58,206 --> 00:03:02,556
<v MR THORNDYKE> Oh, yes, that was in West Park Flats, lovely lady.

10
00:03:02,556 --> 00:03:03,699
<v EDITH> Yes, she is.

11
00:03:03,699 --> 00:03:05,994
<v MR THORNDYKE> And what’s your name, please?

12
00:03:05,994 --> 00:03:07,813
<v EDITH> It’s Edith Pargetter.

13
00:03:07,813 --> 00:03:11,845
<v MR THORNDYKE> Edith … can you spell your surname, please?

14
00:03:11,845 --> 00:03:17,534
<v EDITH> It’s P-A-R-G-E-double T-E-R.

15
00:03:17,534 --> 00:03:22,403
<v MR THORNDYKE> Double T, right. And do you live in West Park Flats as well?

16
00:03:22,403 --> 00:03:26,610
<v EDITH> No, actually it’s East Park, Flat 4.

17
00:03:26,610 --> 00:03:31,561
<v MR THORNDYKE> Oh, right, that’s over the road, I seem to remember – quite difficult to get to.

18
00:03:31,561 --> 00:03:34,680
<v EDITH> Yes, it’s at the back of the library.

19
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:38,136
<v MR THORNDYKE> Right, I know. And what’s your phone number?

20
00:03:38,136 --> 00:03:45,617
<v EDITH> 875934 but I’m out a great deal in the afternoons and evenings.

21
00:03:45,617 --> 00:03:49,172
<v MR THORNDYKE> So would the best time to ring you be in the morning?

22
00:03:49,172 --> 00:03:49,877
<v EDITH> Yes.

23
00:03:49,877 --> 00:03:59,771
<v MR THORNDYKE> Fine. I’ve made a note of that. Can I just ask, I’ll be in a van and I know parking’s rather difficult round your flats. Where would you recommend?

24
00:03:59,771 --> 00:04:08,053
<v EDITH> Well, I always tell people in larger vehicles to park by the postbox on the other side of the road from the entrance.

25
00:04:08,053 --> 00:04:09,487
<v MR THORNDYKE> Good, thanks.

26
00:04:09,487 --> 00:04:13,640
<v EDITH> And will you be able to give me a full itemised quote?

27
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:17,959
<v MR THORNDYKE> Oh, yes, I’ll list all the jobs separately with individual prices. 

28
00:04:17,959 --> 00:04:19,340
<v EDITH> That’d be a great help.

29
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:20,867
<v MR THORNDYKE> No problem.

30
00:05:08,376 --> 00:05:10,408
<v MR THORNDYKE> Now, what would you like me to do?

31
00:05:10,408 --> 00:05:20,967
<v EDITH> Firstly and most urgently is in the kitchen. With all the weather damage, the glass in the door has cracked and I’d need that fixing …

32
00:05:20,967 --> 00:05:23,265
<v MR THORNDYKE> I presume you mean replacing? 

33
00:05:23,265 --> 00:05:25,981
<v EDITH> Oh, yes. And as soon as possible …

34
00:05:25,981 --> 00:05:29,698
<v MR THORNDYKE> What I’ll do is come round tomorrow morning and do that immediately.

35
00:05:29,698 --> 00:05:34,147
<v EDITH> Thank you so much. The other things aren’t so urgent but …

36
00:05:34,147 --> 00:05:37,255
<v MR THORNDYKE> Now, I’ll make a note of everything you want doing.

37
00:05:37,255 --> 00:05:41,525
<v EDITH> Well, in the kitchen I’d like some painting doing. 

38
00:05:41,525 --> 00:05:43,393
<v MR THORNDYKE> All the kitchen walls?

39
00:05:43,393 --> 00:05:47,442
<v EDITH> Just the area over the cooker. It’s very greasy …

40
00:05:47,442 --> 00:05:49,734
<v MR THORNDYKE> Right … it does tend to get that way!

41
00:05:49,734 --> 00:05:50,783
<v EDITH> Yes!

42
00:05:50,783 --> 00:05:58,446
<v MR THORNDYKE> Well, if you want a proper job done what I’d need to do is strip the old paint and plaster it about a week before I paint it.

43
00:05:58,446 --> 00:06:03,408
<v EDITH> Of course. Now, May tells me you also do work in the garden.

44
00:06:03,408 --> 00:06:04,764
<v MR THORNDYKE> That’s right.

45
00:06:04,764 --> 00:06:07,491
<v EDITH> Well, I’d like you to replace a fence.

46
00:06:07,491 --> 00:06:09,231
<v MR THORNDYKE> Just one?

47
00:06:09,231 --> 00:06:11,029
<v EDITH> Yes, at the far end.

48
00:06:11,029 --> 00:06:12,919
<v MR THORNDYKE> Fine. Shouldn’t be a problem. 

49
00:06:12,919 --> 00:06:14,542
<v EDITH> And that’s the lot.

50
00:06:14,542 --> 00:06:20,018
<v MR THORNDYKE> Fine. Yeah, as I say I can come round tomorrow morning to look over things with you.

51
00:06:20,018 --> 00:06:21,497
<v EDITH> That’s great, thank you.

52
00:06:21,497 --> 00:06:25,117
<v MR THORNDYKE> So, I’ll look forward to seeing you tomorrow at …